SWiM_Item,Item_Name,Package_Implementation,Status
1,Grouping studies for synthesis,"Define groups by taxonomy branch, application domain, target property, and architecture.",Ready
2,Standardized metric/transformation,Use R2/RMSE/MAE descriptively; optional Fisher-z transform only if sample sizes and SEs are extractable.,Needs study-level data
3,Synthesis method,Use narrative synthesis plus stratified descriptive statistics; avoid overclaiming pooled meta-analysis where heterogeneity is high.,Ready
4,Criteria to prioritize results,"Prioritize external validation/fabrication validation, larger datasets, independent test sets, and open data.",Ready
5,Heterogeneity investigation,"Stratify by geometry, domain, simulation tool, dataset size, target property, and validation type.",Ready
6,Certainty of evidence,Use QS rubric and sensitivity analysis excluding low-QS/scope-uncertain records.,Template ready
7,Data presentation,"Use summary tables, forest-style plots for comparable groups, and harvest plots for non-comparable metrics.",Ready
8,Reporting results,"Report counts, ranges, medians/IQR, and explicitly label best-reported values.",Ready
9,Limitations,"State publication bias, simulation-only validation, missing open data, and metric heterogeneity.",Ready
